    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0746" n="722" xml:id="pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.F.M. Files: Lot
                    M–88: Box 2061: CFM Documents</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the French
                            Delegation to the Council of Foreign
                            Ministers</hi><anchor n="16" xml:id="d228-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C.F.M.(46) 181</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-02">2 July 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peace Treaty With Italy</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Statute of Trieste</hi></p>
                <p>Trieste and the adjoining district shall form an autonomous territory
                    administered in accordance with a Statute proposed by the four Powers for
                    consideration by the Paris Conference and approval by the United Nations. The
                    United Nations Security Council shall ensure the integrity of the territory.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d228-f1" n="16" type="source" xml:id="d228-f1-content">
                <p>The substance of this proposal was presented by Foreign Minister Bidault at the
                    32nd Meeting of the Council of Foreign Ministers, July 2, and came under
                    consideration by the Council at its 33rd Meeting, July 3; see the United States
                    Delegation Records of these meetings, <ref target="#pg715">pp. 715</ref> and
                        <ref target="#pg730">730</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
